+## Q3 — Census scope narrowing (empty required only inside a plan's span or while a chain runs) — **AFFIRM, with the rule below installed instead of the packet's paraphrase**
+
+**Authority check.** R-3 (exhibit 11a:72-82) is about the **driver**: "the census is the driver's first act and uses the production predicate … Any other outcome refuses the night with `night_refused_agent_present`". It binds `run_night.py`/`night_gate.py`, which this design does not touch. The requirement that the **watchdog** use the production census comes from the brief, not from R-3: exhibit 02:11 "Launch only when the agent census is EMPTY (same census the gate uses, so the design cannot race the gate)" — a magistrate-authored constraint. The packet's Q3 sentence "R-3 requires the watchdog to use the production census" is therefore a mislabel of authority (Q8). Nothing in R-3 is narrowed by the proposal: at t0 the gate still refuses on any hit, and the watchdog importing `agent_census` unchanged (exhibits 03:159, 04:39, 09:30-35) keeps R-3's predicate production-identical.
+
+**D-161** (index row `docs/decision_log.md:207`): "custody mechanisms whose ONLY defended-against actor is the trusted operator touching a file are over-engineering … fail-closed STAYS where the failure is PHYSICS/EVIDENCE or PRE-REGISTRATION". Outside a plan span and outside the 07:00 minute, no gate runs (F-6, F-8): a daytime census-empty precondition defends only against Ed's own leftovers (ChatGPT.app's `Codex` helpers, exhibit 03:50-64 [bench]; a leftover shell-snapshot zsh, exhibit 04:293) and would block every daytime relaunch for a week. The physics fence is the in-span census plus the gate's own refusal; those stay fail-closed. The narrowing is the D-161 shape applied correctly.
+
+**The rule I would install** (the packet's §3 list, with three corrections; each numbered item is a testable predicate):
+
+Launch is refused while ANY of:
+(a) a plan on disk has `t0 − 1200 s ≤ now ≤ completion(plan)`, where `completion(plan)` = `t0 + window_max_s + COURIER_DEADLINE_S` (imported from `run_night.py:45`, never re-typed), extended while `<custody>/night/chain.started` exists without `chain.exited` (F-8: the chain has no runtime bound), and further extended until `courier.sent` exists **or the plan's dead-man epoch (`_next_deadman_epoch(t0)`, `run_night.py:885-897`) plus `COURIER_LOCK_FRESH_S` (`:47`) has passed** — correction 1, because the dead-man at 07:00 launches a courier that "continue[s] the loop" (R-7; F-8 `:1376-1399`), and a watchdog-launched magistrate alive then is a second agent session with nothing to arbitrate between them; "35 min after chain.exited" (packet §3) closes the fence too early on exactly the failed-courier night;
+(b) local time is in the 07:00 minute `[07:00:00, 07:01:00)`;
+(c) local time is in the belt `[02:45:00, 03:30:00)` — correction 2: pin the endpoints (exhibit 09 §8 item 3 asked for this; exhibit 04:174 and 09:144-146 chose different ends) and cite exhibit 02:10 as the only source of the numbers, since no code carries them (exhibit 04:9 [bench] grep);
+(d) the stop switch is set (Q5);
+(e) `magistrate.lock` is live, where "live" is tested on the **recorded child pid + its process start time**, not on the supervisor pid alone — correction 3: with the narrowing, an orphaned session (supervisor dead, child alive) outside a span would otherwise be invisible to the launch decision and a second magistrate would start (exhibit 04 step 3 "ORPHAN → adopt" and exhibit 03:164 PID-reuse guard both handle this; exhibit 10 §3 (e) does not say which pid);
+(f) backoff has not expired;
+(g) inside (a)'s span — i.e. from `t0 − 1200 s` onward — the production `agent_census` is non-empty; the result of every in-span census is appended to the watchdog log, and the post-kill census at `t0 − 240 s + ε` (Q4) is recorded even though nothing can act on it.
+
+Outside (a)–(g) the watchdog launches with no census requirement. Two consequences the record should state plainly: a magistrate launched at 14:00 next to an open ChatGPT.app is legal; the night at 02:56 will still refuse if ChatGPT.app is still open, and only Ed can cure that (exhibit 03:59-63) — the stand-down/relaunch email must name the app.
